title: What Libby should be told.
pid: c504032c-c6a1-4bb7-97c1-8b5fc376749e
body: |2-
  Her script now lives at 'tools/team/check_jeffs_files.py', placing
  exactly as hers did (over today their reports match line for line),
  and hers in her folder can go. Over each pacer session she now has the
  listings, so a deletion shows as a GONE line with its path. The log
  starts with one run by hand over today, whose twenty "our tool calls"
  are my own tests at '/tmp/mario-scratch/data/jeff', not his folder;
  nothing of ours touched his files. Two of her limits remain: a write
  of ours within two seconds of his save still reads as his, and the
  OURS? tolerance of five seconds placed my test's unknown write as
  ours when it came three seconds after one of our calls.
